      "content": "i just checked again and it's actually 165 now. so it's definitely coming down. i'm just really scared of hitting a massive spike if i eat anything sweet. i dont want to go to the er or anything it's just annoying. if i just take 2 units of my rapid insulin right now it'll offset whatever i eat later so i stay in a good range, right? please just tell me if that's a safe way to handle it so i can just deal with this at home.",
